WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 18 - The Role of the Doll

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.930
"My body has always been weak and there were times when they thought I'd die...

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.180
but now I'm dying for real!"

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:50.530
"Mother and Father died in a plane crash but they're calling out to me!"

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:51.880
"Miss Marissa!"

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.240
"There's only one thing that worries me..."

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.620
I wish I had some lines too.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.250
Being a lifeless doll is so hard.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.760
After that line, look at the doll.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.880
Ma'am, we're supposed to be mindful of your health and limit rehearsals to a maximum of two hours.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:11.680
The doctor told us...

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.860
Don't worry about me!

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.770
Now, Taiko, push down on the doll's shoulders.

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:15.740
Got it.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.290
"How come the doll inherits everything?!"

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.460
"How stupid!"

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.500
Maya!

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.470
You're not moving like a doll would!

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:28.550
Like a doll would?

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.830
If you push a person, they can resist,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.980
but a doll falls over instantly!

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.810
Taiko, I want you to push Maya's shoulder again.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.080
Okay.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.090
What was your back doing then?!

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.050
Does a doll just fall over by itself?

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.150
Do it again!

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.360
Again!

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.250
Again!

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.100
Keep your arms and legs stiff!

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.920
Don't open your eyes wider!

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.480
A doll has no expression.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.050
Start again!

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:18.850
How on earth can a doll frown?

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.640
Do it again!

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.980
Ms. Tsukikage - what are you doing here?

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.060
I've been given permission to leave the hospital for the day.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.010
But...

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.930
Let's continue with our rehearsal.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.460
So, here you are.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.090
Let's get you back to the hospital, Ms. Tsukikage.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.050
We can't have you dying on us.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.360
Maya!

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:45.320
Maya.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.400
Get up by yourself.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.170
Maya!

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.310
Stop! Leave her alone!

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:07.480
Maya!

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.540
What happened?!

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.420
We have to take your clothes off!

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:09.960
No!

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.110
What's the meaning of this, Ms. Tsukikage?!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.060
She must learn how to play a doll.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:38.370
University Hospital

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.440
You're completely mad.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.390
Both of you.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:41.460
This is something you couldn't possibly understand, Mr. Masumi.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:46.140
You don't understand the happiness of following your passion with conviction.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.610
I was once like you.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.450
When I first met the playwright, Ichiren Ozaki, and started...

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:57.190
studying acting, it was as though I had finally found my reason to live.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.260
It was a hard road, but I was happy.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:08.200
Ichiren Ozaki taught me that when you have something to live for,

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.980
you value yourself as a person.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:15.960
I want to live. I want to keep on living as long as there are plays to be performed.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:21.040
Were you in love with Ichiren Ozaki?

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.710
If it wasn't for my love of the stage, I would have broken down...

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:27.730
when he died.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:32.680
Your father is the man who drove him to suicide!

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.460
Eisuke Hayami!

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.720
I need to talk to you.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.180
I also must apologize for hurting you the other day.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.340
How are you getting along, little one?

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:07.350
Once I graduate, I plan to study acting while working part-time.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:09.160
If you want to continue acting,

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.870
it would help to have a broader knowledge of other subjects as well.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.460
You should seriously consider continuing on to high school.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.580
Don't you think I realize that?!

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.980
But it's impossible!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.340
You could become a Daito Theater actress.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.450
Your board, your school expenses - all of it would be covered.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.340
You need to think about your future.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.970
You need to get away from Ms. Tsukikage!

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.590
And if I tell you I don't want to?

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.600
Are you really prepared to make me your enemy?

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.760
Yes.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.340
You'll regret it.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:36.930
I would rather die!

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:39.780
I don't care what kind of life I have to lead instead...

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:43.130
I will <i>never</i> accept help from the Daito Theater!

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.850
If you don't leave this instant, I'm going to hit you!

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:46.700
Ow...

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:50.340
Take care, little one.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.740
It's not like I don't want to go to high school. I really do.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.460
But I just can't.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:02.730
He's just trying to play to my weaknesses.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.970
So you'd rather die, would you?

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.480
High school?

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:15.310
One Star Academy is renowned for its acting talent.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:18.470
The person I told you about has agreed to pay for all your expenses.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:22.300
But who'd do that for little old me?

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:26.140
Hm... I only had the opportunity to speak to a representative of theirs,

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.990
but it seems like this person holds your talent for acting in very high regard.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.730
I was told to give you this.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.090
A purple rose...

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.850
Mr. or Mrs. Purple Rose!

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.650
"Please accept this."

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:45.850
"I am looking forward to your improvement as an actress."

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:47.520
"From: Your Fan."

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:48.620
Whoever it is,

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:51.670
they're really looking forward to the day you become a world-class actress!

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:54.450
I'm going to do it, Mr. or Mrs. Purple Rose!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:59.590
I'm going to become a world-class actress!

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.390
Okay, let's meet this Sunday!

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.860
You never have time usually. This is wonderful!

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.450
I've wanted to go and see that movie for ages.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.100
Hey, there's a new donut store down by the station.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.950
It's supposed to be really good. Wanna go?

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:15.680
Sakurakouji, there's this part I didn't get on my homework...

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.160
and I was wondering if you might...

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.250
Sakurakouji...

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.040
Sure, no problem.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.160
Oh, thank you!

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.290
Maya!

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.310
I saw you from the window, so I hopped off.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.170
I wanted to return your umbrella.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:46.420
I'll walk you to the station.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.360
There are so many things I want to say to him,

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:57.430
but, in the end, I can't say a word.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.390
I'll come in with you.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.860
Sakurakouji!

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:10.350
He hasn't changed one bit!

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.260
I really liked <i>Wuthering Heights</i>.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.350
Thank you!

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:18.850
I was really jealous of Heathcliff, though.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.850
Sakurakouji...

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:31.430
There's something different about him, though.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.850
Something's different...

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.330
Café

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:41.020
They say it used to be a café, but it went out of business.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:44.400
Now they want to turn this space into a stage!

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.890
Would anyone come to a place like this?

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:51.640
It's nothing fancy, that's for sure, but the rent is cheap.

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:54.010
So, let's start cleaning this place up!

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:59.420
They don't seriously think they can make that basement into a stage!

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:03.910
For a start, they'd be competing with the Orion Stage just across the street!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.890
People will just carry on coming here and their place will go under again.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.420
I wonder.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.870
Ayumi Himekawa...

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:17.380
Do you have any idea who's renting that basement?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.090
Does it matter? They're some nameless troupe.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.250
Yes, it does. They may not have a name,

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.890
but that doesn't mean they're talentless.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:28.640
Ikkakujuu,the troupe that took second place in the National Acting Competition,

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.910
and the winners of the popular vote,

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:35.130
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe, are renting out that space.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.030
But they're still amateurs!

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.910
And that place doesn't even have proper facilities!

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:44.670
Acting doesn't depend on facilities.

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:48.040
It depends on skill. And one of those people happens to be...

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.160
Maya Kitajima.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.890
Maya Kitajima?

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:53.700
I've heard of her...

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:56.370
Isn't she the one that the Eishinza's Kikuko Harada...

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:57.890
gave the nickname "The Stage Storm"?

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:04.120
Just make sure your stage isn't the one getting stormed.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:17.040
The audience have to sit on mats and benches, do they?

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.950
We'll make it up to them with our acting!

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.480
Yeah!

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:24.580
"What are you saying?"

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.490
"You want to marry a doll?!"

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:29.970
"That's right! I love her!"

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:32.970
"I'll never take another wife!"

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:35.240
"Are you mad, Pio?"

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.970
I want to act too.

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:42.820
I hope Ms. Tsukikage gets better soon.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.010
I wonder how Sakurakouji is getting on with his plays.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:51.040
Mom... she doesn't even know our troupe disbanded...

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:54.280
or that I'm living in an apartment now.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:58.370
Just wait a little longer, Mom! I'll become an actress and then...

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.650
That's what Ms. Tsukikage would have done if she were here.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.680
Maya, a doll can't stare into space like that!

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:09.180
I'm sorry. Sitting around with nothing to do makes my mind wander.

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:15.190
You've played a lot of roles up to this point. But now, you're a doll.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.750
A doll has no soul.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:21.250
It has no soul.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:28.210
Why did Ms. Tsukikage give her a role that has no movement or lines?

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:35.130
We feel bad about this whole thing,

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.340
but we just can't let you carry on when you're in this state.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:40.860
Miss Haru, why don't you check yourself into a health clinic,

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.610
where you can get some fresh air?

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:48.840
If it's a matter of money, we can see to that.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.610
After all, you've worked for us for a long, long time.

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:54.710
And if your health improves, you can come back and work for us again!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.600
That sounds good, doesn't it?

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.260
Yeah...

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.310
Then,

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:05.780
that's what I'll do.

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:10.760
Thank you for supporting me for all these years.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.750
If Maya happens to come back here...

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:16.800
Don't worry. I'll let her know where you are.

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.830
It's been two years since she ran away from home.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:31.190
I've told myself so many times that I don't need a daughter like you, but even so...

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:36.210
I've never forgotten you - not for a moment.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:39.520
You are my only daughter.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.080
Excuse me.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.640
The Hidden Star?!
It's Cathy!
Acting? Really? What passion!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.780
Maya? Maya!

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.110
That's Maya! That's Maya!

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:58.200
No doubt about it.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.310
Hey! That's my daughter!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.380
My daughter! Here, look at this photo!

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:08.550
You ran away and said you were going to become an actress.

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:10.690
But here you are on stage with your picture in a magazine!

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:13.870
You've grown taller, haven't you?

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:18.180
That girl...

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:22.080
Here, take this.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:24.550
Thank you very much.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.610
Your back is bent.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:44.730
Ma'am, why have you sent me to a Zen temple?

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:48.360
Reaching a state of nonexistence is very difficult.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.610
Consider that rock.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.030
That rock has no doubts.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.810
It has no hardships.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:58.920
If we can think of ourselves as that rock, we can become that rock.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:04.300
Listen to the sound of the wind and melt into the green carpet of the earth.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:10.200
Then we can forget that we are human; we can forget our desires,

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:14.260
and our faces will become devoid of expression.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.010
Become a rock.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.400
A rock. A rock.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:22.160
A heart of stone.

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:29.170
Everyone! Come one, come all! The show starts at six-thirty!

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:29.160
The Stone's Smile

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:32.190
Look at them rounding up passersby like it's some kind of carnival!

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:34.790
I heard that they only have mats to sit on over there!

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:37.300
You're kidding!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:45.660
The Stone's Smile

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.520
We don't seem to be selling any tickets.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.300
I'd like one.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:45.670
Here you go!

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:52.310
Is the play starting yet?!

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.290
Ayumi's here.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:59.070
Are we putting this play on for our own enjoyment or for theirs?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.320
Right. Let the show begin!

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:09.460
What's going on?

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:15.100
We're experiencing some turbulence and would ask that all passengers...

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.960
please fasten their seatbelts for the time being.

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:28.410
...but now I'm dying for real!

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:30.750
Mother and Father died in a plane crash but they're calling out to me!

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:32.230
Miss Marissa!

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:35.060
There's only one thing that worries me...

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:39.410
I've always been weak and have never had any friends... except one.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.990
Elizabeth.

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:45.000
What will happen to her if I die?

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:51.140
I've written my will and I'm now giving it to you as my lawyer.

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:54.880
Please make sure it's followed to the letter.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:04.940
I want to thank everyone for coming today.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:07.570
I am the lawyer who has been entrusted with...

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:08.910
What the...

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.270
Why is she playing a doll?

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:16.340
Ayumi's here. And Mashima too!

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:23.730
The president of the great English conglomerate, Sir Bartholomew and his wife are deceased.

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:28.230
Shortly thereafter, their daughter also passed away.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.760
I will now read the final will of Miss Marissa.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.220
"I hereby leave all of my assets to my beloved Elizabeth."

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.240
She wants to leave it all to that doll?!

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:40.570
The entire fortune of the Bartholomew family?!

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:42.330
That doll sure is large!

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.860
That's because it's being played by a real person!

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:44.590
You can't be serious!

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:47.820
"And finally, if anyone can demonstrate that they love Elizabeth wholeheartedly...

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:51.590
then they will become sole executors to the aforementioned assets."

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:52.880
Sole executors?

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.440
"If no one meets these conditions, my estate along with Elizabeth...

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:58.170
will be donated to a museum."

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:01.600
"And if anyone who cares for her hurts or damages her in any way,

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.590
they lose all rights as executors."

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:14.810
I have to look after this doll every day. It's so ridiculous.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:25.880
You can stay there for now, Miss Heiress. I have cleaning to do.

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:31.330
She doesn't move a muscle, yet her whole body is acting.

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:34.260
This doll is the very soul of the play!

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.630
If, at any point, she gives even the slightest impression that she's actually human,

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.370
this whole play will fall apart.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:42.880
What must I do to become her guardian?

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:46.710
Those who desired the estate finally decided to consult a fortune teller.

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:51.420
She's a slight girl with blond hair and blue eyes.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.130
She can't talk nor move - she just sits there.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.560
She can't move?

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:59.130
How can I demonstrate my love for her?

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:00.200
I <i>must</i> know...

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:06.210
Your best option is to put her in a wheelchair.

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.130
Take her out for walks...

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:11.390
and show how devoted you are to her.

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.200
My deceased niece was very fond of her.

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.200
She loved her as if she were human.

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:17.790
As if she were human?

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:20.310
She often changed her clothes...

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.230
Changed her clothes?

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:24.460
Did she think she was some kind of upper-class pet?

00:19:26.670 --> 00:19:29.950
Freedom is the most important thing to remember.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:33.760
You can show your love by mimicking your niece's actions.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.050
Mimicking my niece?

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.510
So I should play house with a doll?

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:41.320
So how can we prove that we love her?

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.560
It's not like she can talk.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.130
A common problem when it comes to love!

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:50.020
What you really need is an engagement ring!

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:52.040
Isn't proposing the most lavish expression of love?

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:55.650
Marry Elizabeth?!

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:03.590
Marriage. I see. I didn't even consider that.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.620
That's definitely a possibility.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.760
That was pretty good!

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.750
Rei Aoki is so great!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.430
And what a pretty-looking doll!

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:37.490
Too bad for you, I won this round.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.560
You put on a great show!

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:44.100
Everyone's pacing was great!

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:46.760
You all work really well together.

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:53.770
Together? She's right, Sayaka and Rei work well together.

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.820
Up until now, I've always acted alone.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:00.310
I thought that, as long as I performed well, everything would fall into place,

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:03.750
but I shouldn't think like that. You can't act in a vacuum.

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:09.860
The doll. So that's why Ms. Tsukikage made me play a doll.

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:14.790
She wanted to teach me the act of smothering my real self!

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.790
The Stone's Smile

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:19.500
News of their performance spread by word of mouth,

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:22.100
and their audience grew larger by the day.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:25.080
And then, on the tenth night...

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.300
What's happening down there?!

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:32.490
How on earth could this happen?

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:37.000
Please, don't push!

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:37.000
Are there are any tickets left?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.760
I'm sorry. We're all sold out!

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:42.340
Not even Maya could believe what she was seeing.

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:47.250
But she couldn't even imagine the news she would soon receive,

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:49.760
completely out of the blue.

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
Asa kara yoru made yoru kara asa made

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
From morning until night, from dusk till dawn,

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
Futari ai no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
you can feel the warmth of our love.

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
Shunkashuutou mo ippun ichibyou mo

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
All year round, every minute and every second,

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
Futari hada no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
you can feel the warmth of our skin.

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
Kono dokidoki wa makka ni moeru taiyou

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
This excitement is burning brightly like the sun,

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
Atsuku moete atsuku togashite

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
let us burn brightly, let us burn until we're hot

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
Koi wo shimashou!

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
and make love!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Sunao na mama dakiaou!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Let's hold and be true to each other!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
Isso mekimeki nekki! mekimeki daisuki!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
And let's add more heat! I love the heat!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Aishiae!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Feel the love!

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:26.190
Sumiko has told me that my mom has gone missing.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:30.000
I didn't even know you were sick, Mom!

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.000
And then, even though he always come to my plays,

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:35.350
Sakurakouji hasn't shown up this time...

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:37.750
Majima, my co-star from <i>Wuthering Heights</i>,

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:41.340
has been saying strange things to me because he thinks I'm Cathy.

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:46.100
It feels like all the people I cherish are disappearing.

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:50.250
With all these feelings swirling around inside my head, can I still manage to play a lifeless doll?

00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 19 - A Mask Removed
